Hmmm, I think this works (skill notetag):
<JS Post-Apply>
let stateId = 0;
if (target.states().length > 0) {
for (let i = 0; i < target.states().length; i++) {
stateId = target.states()[i].id;
if (target.states()[i].meta["Negative State"]){
target.setStateTurns(stateId, target.stateTurns(stateId)+2);
}
}
}
</JS Post-Apply>
EDIT: You have to mark your negative states with the <Negative State> notetag.
